  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 1243 PM CDT Wed Sep 2 2026\n\nThe Heat Advisory is still in effect through Saturday and ends \nat 8 PM that evening. It is possible that the advisory gets\nextended through the holiday weekend, though there is a backdoor\ncold front moving through the area on Sunday. It may sound like\nfall weather is on the way, but it's not. The airmass through\nthe weekend won't likely change all that much despite the front\nmoving through. It'll still feel hot if you're participating in\nany outdoor activities this weekend. Remember the rest of the \nweek into the weekend will feature a Major to Extreme HeatRisk \nacross our area. Be sure to hydrate and take breaks from the \nheat this weekend, especially with no overnight relief. The\nExtreme HeatRisk does start to back off going into the start of\nnext week. Very low-end POPs of 15-30% move into the area on \nSunday due to the incoming front. No signal for appreciable\nrainfall through the end of the long term period and Monday and\nTuesday will be in the mid 90s.",
